ac_md5*` tripped Rust's debug-only \"misaligned pointer","+   dereference\" check (`SIGABRT`) where the C simply performs the unaligned","+   access. The byte-granular accessors (`ld_u32`/`st_u32`/`ld_u64`/`st_u64`","+   with `from_ne_bytes`/`to_ne_bytes`) removed the difference, and are","+   endian-neutral, so the translation stays correct on big-endian targets too.","+","+No behavioural divergence was found on any valid input (Phase B)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
